course: dictionary
lesson: 10012
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives both, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Read the words around the word, then ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: «Temple» is a good example. In «When Jesus was twelve he stayed behind in the Temple in Jerusalem», the Temple is a building where people go to pray and worship. Think of a place of worship, and the sentence makes sense.
explain: Now look at the other meaning. Your temple is the flat part of your head, on each side, between your eye and your ear. Health lessons teach that this soft part must be protected, which is one reason we wear helmets. A bump there is a clue that the word means your head, not a building.
fact: A temple is a building where people go to pray and worship.
fact: Temples are found in religions such as Hinduism, Buddhism, Sikhism and Judaism, and in ancient religions.
fact: Your temple is the flat part of your head, between your eye and your ear.
fact: «Uruk, about 5,000 years ago, had ... big temples and city walls, and is one of the first real cities in the world.»
fact: A good check is to swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Uruk, about 5,000 years ago, had tens of thousands of people, big temples and city walls, and is one of the first real cities in the world.» In this sentence, what is a temple? | A city wall | *A building where people worship | The flat part of the head beside the eye | A kind of farm
exercise: «Ruth was the great-grandmother of King David; ... his son Solomon built the Temple in Jerusalem.» Who built the Temple in Jerusalem? | Goliath | Mao | *Solomon | Ruth
exercise: «She rubbed her temple after the bump on the head.» Which meaning fits here? | A holiday in the sun | A place where people pray | A type of city wall | *The flat part of the head beside the eye
test: «When Jesus was twelve he stayed behind in the Temple in Jerusalem asking and answering questions.» Where was the Temple? | On the side of the head | In a helmet | *In Jerusalem | In Uruk
test: The health lesson says the temple must be protected. Which part of the body is it? | Your knee | Your elbow | Your stomach | *The flat part of your head between your eye and ear
exam: When a word has two meanings, what should you do? | Skip the sentence and move on without thinking | Guess, because it does not matter | Always pick the first meaning you ever learned | *Read the words around it and try each meaning in the sentence to see which one makes sense
